menu "ups-adaptor board"

choice UPSA_BOARD
    prompt "Target board"
    default UPSA_BOARD_REV_A
    help
        Selects the pin map and peripheral set.

        Rev A is the reference target: it is what the hardware design, the
        pin map and the feature set are built around. The Freenove devkit is
        a development fallback so firmware can be built and run before Rev A
        boards exist, and it is missing hardware Rev A has -- notably the
        VBUS load switch and the status LEDs.

        Application code must never reference a GPIO number directly. Use
        the BOARD_* macros from board.h.

config UPSA_BOARD_REV_A
    bool "ups-adaptor Rev A PCB (reference target)"

config UPSA_BOARD_FREENOVE
    bool "Freenove ESP32-S3-WROOM devkit (development fallback)"

endchoice

config UPSA_HAVE_OLED
    bool "Enable optional I2C OLED status display"
    default n
    help
        The web interface is the primary UI. The OLED is a debug convenience
        and is the single most expensive item on the BOM, so it is off by
        default. Rev A keeps the footprint; firmware does not require it.

config UPSA_VBUS_CYCLE_MS
    int "VBUS off-time when power-cycling a wedged UPS interface (ms)"
    default 2000
    range 250 10000

endmenu
